All builds include SyncTERM Emoji, rasterized from Noto Emoji under the SIL
Open Font License 1.1. Its copyright notice and full license are retained in
`src/media/fonts/LICENSE.NOTO-EMOJI` and the in-program Licenses viewer.

When `SYNCTERM_ENABLE_UNIFONT` is enabled, the executable includes the
SyncTERM Unicode font, derived from GNU Unifont and UNSCII, under the SIL
Open Font License 1.1. See `src/media/unifont/UPSTREAM.md` and
`src/media/unifont/LICENSE.OFL-1.1` for its copyright notices and full license.
Bundled notices are available in the program under SyncTERM Settings > Licenses.

The protocol-checksum component in src/base/md5/ is derived from the RSA Data
Security, Inc. MD5 Message-Digest Algorithm and retains that component's
separate notice in src/base/md5/LICENSE.

